   "gap_before": 0.88,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "sleep.dlg17"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Stomach, mostly. Face squished into the pillow.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.85,
   "block": "sleep.dlg17",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Stomach sleeping can arch your lower back. Try putting a flat pillow under your hips, or slowly training yourself onto your side.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.84,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "sleep.dlg17"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Side with",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.86,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "sleep.dlg17"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "a pillow between my knees?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 2.17,
   "block": "sleep.dlg17",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Exactly that. It keeps your hips level and takes pressure off your back.",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.91,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "sleep.dlg17"
  },
  {
